 quite small ...", "id": 2, "time": "22000", "image": "engenn7le10ob09re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Rachel</span>:    You could try resetting the router. It may be a firmware issue.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    Could you explain to me what that means?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Rachel</span>:    It's a piece of software that runs the router. You should make sure all the lights are green. If they aren't, I would switch  the router off and go back to the factory preset.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:    Let me check. Oh no! The lights are all off.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Rachel</span>:    It may be a hardware issue in that case.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Great  ...", "id": 3, "time": "41000", "image": "engenn7le10ob09re2img01.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le10ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le10ob09re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}